# $title

Write a Python script that reads whitespace-separated integers from standard input and
prints one line: the length of the longest run of consecutive numbers where each number is
strictly greater than the one before it.

## Rules

- No input numbers means no run: print `0`.
- A single number is a run of length `1`.
- Equal neighbors end a run: for `1 2 2 3` the runs are `1 2` and `2 3`, so print `2`.
- Use only the standard library. Print nothing else.

## Examples

| stdin       | stdout |
|-------------|--------|
| `1 2 3 1 2` | `3`    |
| `5 4 3`     | `1`    |
| (empty)     | `0`    |
